# 21. DETECTING UNAUTHORIZED SSIDS

Suppose the authorized list is:

```text
NAVLAN
NAVLAN-GUEST
NAVLAN-IOT
```

The monitoring system observes:

```text
NAVLAN
NAVLAN-GUEST
NAVLAN-IOT
FREE-WIFI
NAVLAN-FREE
```

The unexpected SSIDs should be investigated.

---

# 22. MAC ADDRESS MONITORING

Each wireless interface normally has a MAC address.

A WIDS can maintain an inventory:

```text
AP-01 → AA:AA:AA:AA:AA:01
AP-02 → AA:AA:AA:AA:AA:02
AP-03 → AA:AA:AA:AA:AA:03
```

If a new BSSID appears:

```text
AA:AA:AA:AA:AA:99
```

the system can generate:

> **Unknown AP detected**

---

# 23. MAC SPOOFING

An attacker may attempt to imitate an authorized MAC address.

Therefore:

> **MAC address alone should not be treated as a perfect identity.**

Use multiple indicators:

```text
MAC
+
SSID
+
Channel
+
Signal
+
Security configuration
+
Physical location
+
Network connection
```

---

# 24. SIGNAL STRENGTH

Signal strength can provide useful clues.

Example:

```text
Authorized AP:
RSSI ≈ -60 dBm

Unexpected AP:
RSSI ≈ -20 dBm
```

A very strong unexpected signal may indicate an AP physically close to the monitored area.

But:

> Signal strength does not prove malicious intent.

---

# 25. LOCATION ANALYSIS

If the organization knows where APs are physically installed:

```text
AP-01 → Building A, Floor 1
AP-02 → Building A, Floor 2
AP-03 → Building B, Floor 1
```

An unknown AP can be investigated using:

- Signal strength
- Multiple sensors
- Direction/location techniques
- Physical inspection
- Switch-port information

---

# 26. CHANNEL ANOMALIES

Suppose authorized APs use:

```text
Channel 1
Channel 6
Channel 11
```

A new device suddenly appears on an unexpected channel.

Possible reasons:

- Neighboring network
- Legitimate AP
- Temporary device
- Misconfiguration
- Rogue AP

Therefore:

> Channel anomaly = investigate, not automatically attack.

---

# 27. SECURITY CONFIGURATION

An organization might require:

```text
WPA2-Enterprise
```

but monitoring detects:

```text
Same SSID
Open network
```

This is a strong indicator requiring investigation.

Compare:

```text
SSID
BSSID
Authentication
Encryption
Channel
```

---

# 28. OPEN WI-FI DETECTION

If a protected organizational SSID suddenly appears as an open network:

```text
Company-WiFi
Security: Open
```

while the authorized configuration is:

```text
Company-WiFi
Security: WPA2/WPA3 Enterprise
```

this is suspicious.

