# 57. IMPORTANT DISTINCTION

### Rogue AP

Unauthorized AP connected to/within the organizational environment.

### Evil Twin

AP impersonating or mimicking a legitimate wireless network.

They can overlap, but they are not identical concepts.

---

# 58. EVIL TWIN VS ROGUE AP

| Rogue AP | Evil Twin |
|---|---|
| Unauthorized AP | Impersonating/mimicking legitimate network |
| May use different SSID | Often uses same/similar SSID |
| Main concern unauthorized device | Main concern deception |
| Could be accidental or malicious | Usually malicious/unauthorized |

---

# 59. DEAUTH VS EVIL TWIN

### Deauthentication

Goal:

> Disrupt/force disconnection.

### Evil Twin

Goal:

> Impersonate a legitimate network and potentially attract clients.

An attacker may combine techniques, but they are different attack concepts.

