# 64. WIRESHARK AND WIRELESS

Wireshark can analyze captured wireless frames when the capture setup provides suitable 802.11 traffic.

Potentially useful protocol/filter areas include:

```text
wlan
```

and wireless management/control/data frames.

Depending on the capture environment and driver, monitor mode and radiotap metadata may be available.

---

# 65. IMPORTANT WIRESHARK CONCEPT

A normal Ethernet capture:

```text
Ethernet → IP → TCP
```

A wireless capture may provide:

```text
Radiotap
   ↓
802.11
   ↓
LLC/SNAP
   ↓
IP
   ↓
TCP
```

The exact layers depend on the capture method.

