# 77. EXAM TRAPS

### Trap 1

> "Same SSID = Evil Twin."

❌ False.

Multiple legitimate APs can use the same SSID.

---

### Trap 2

> "Unknown AP = confirmed attacker."

❌ False.

It may be a neighboring AP, temporary device, or authorized but undocumented AP.

---

### Trap 3

> "One deauthentication packet proves an attack."

❌ False.

Deauthentication can occur legitimately.

---

### Trap 4

> "MAC address proves device identity."

❌ False.

MAC addresses can be spoofed/changed.

---

### Trap 5

> "WIDS prevents attacks."

❌ Not primarily.

WIDS focuses on **detection and alerting**. WIPS adds prevention capabilities.

