# 80. DAY 34 MASTER CONCEPT

The most important idea today is:

> **Wireless intrusion detection is not about identifying one "bad packet." It is about establishing a normal wireless baseline, monitoring APs and clients, detecting anomalies, correlating multiple indicators, validating the evidence, and responding appropriately.**

```text
NORMAL BASELINE
      ↓
MONITOR
      ↓
ANOMALY
      ↓
CORRELATE
      ↓
VALIDATE
      ↓
INVESTIGATE
      ↓
RESPOND
```

# ⭐ ONE-LINE EXAM ANSWER

> **Wireless Intrusion Detection (WIDS) monitors wireless networks for unauthorized APs, suspicious clients, abnormal authentication/association activity, management-frame anomalies, and other indicators of wireless attacks, generating alerts for investigation.**

# 🏆 DAY 34 GOLDEN RULE

> **Never classify a wireless event from a single indicator alone. Combine SSID, BSSID, security configuration, channel, signal, timing, location, authentication events, and network context before declaring an attack.**